proof_plan:
Collect the orthonormal eigenvectors into $\mathbf Q = \begin {bmatrix} \mathbf q_1 & \cdots & \mathbf q_n \end {bmatrix}$ and the eigenvalues into $\mathbf D$.
Then $\mathbf A \mathbf Q = \mathbf Q \mathbf D$, so $\mathbf A = \mathbf Q \mathbf D \mathbf Q^\intercal$, which is the [[Spectral Theorem for Real Symmetric Matrices|spectral theorem]].
{{qed}}
